  1294|  1294|### C. Companion Planting Guide
  1295|  1295|
  1296|  1296|**Good companions for perennial crops:**
  1297|  1297|- **Jerusalem artichoke:** Comfrey, yarrow, borage (attract beneficial insects)
  1298|  1298|- **Good King Henry:** Comfrey, nitrogen-fixing plants
  1299|  1299|- **Welsh onion:** Carrots, lettuce, strawberries
  1300|  1300|- **Sorrel:** Chives, mint (repel pests)
  1301|  1301|- **Asparagus:** Tomatoes (repel asparagus beetles)
  1302|  1302|- **Rhubarb:** Strawberries, beans
  1303|  1303|- **Sea Kale:** Native coastal plants
  1304|  1304|- **Turkish rocket:** Peas, beans (nitrogen fixers)
  1305|  1305|- **Daubenton's Kale:** Peas, beans, aromatic herbs
  1306|  1306|
  1307|  1307|### D. Troubleshooting Guide
  1308|  1308|
  1309|  1309|| Problem | Likely Cause | Solution |
  1310|  1310||---------|--------------|----------|
  1311|  1311|| Yellowing leaves | Nutrient deficiency | Top-dress with compost |
  1312|  1312|| Poor yield | Overcrowding | Divide plants |
  1313|  1313|| Pest damage | Lack of beneficial insects | Plant companion flowers |
  1314|  1314|| Root rot | Poor drainage | Improve drainage or raise beds |
  1315|  1315|| Failure to establish | Planting too deep/shallow | Adjust planting depth |
  1316|  1316|| Leggy growth | Insufficient light | Move to sunnier location |
