  1556|  1556|## 21. Economic and Social Benefits
  1557|  1557|
  1558|  1558|### Individual Benefits
  1559|  1559|- **Food security:** Reliable food source independent of grocery stores
  1560|  1560|- **Health:** Fresh, nutrient-dense produce
  1561|  1561|- **Savings:** Reduced grocery bills (30-70% reduction)
  1562|  1562|- **Exercise:** Moderate physical activity in the garden
  1563|  1563|- **Mental health:** Connection to nature, sense of accomplishment
  1564|  1564|
  1565|  1565|### Community Benefits
  1566|  1566|- **Local food systems:** Reduced food miles
  1567|  1567|- **Genetic diversity:** Preservation of heirloom varieties
  1568|  1568|- **Education:** Teaching children where food comes from
  1569|  1569|- **Resilience:** Community food security in crisis
  1570|  1570|
  1571|  1571|### Environmental Benefits
  1572|  1572|- **Carbon sequestration:** Building soil organic matter
  1573|  1573|- **Water conservation:** Reduced irrigation needs
  1574|  1574|- **Biodiversity:** Habitat for wildlife
  1575|  1575|- **Reduced chemical inputs:** No synthetic fertilizers or pesticides needed
  1576|  1576|
