  1662|  1662|
  1663|  1663|## 24. Glossary of Terms
  1664|  1664|
  1665|  1665|**Perennial:** A plant that lives for more than two years and produces flowers and fruit repeatedly.
  1666|  1666|
  1667|  1667|**Biennial:** A plant that completes its life cycle in two years (grows leaves first year, flowers and seeds second year).
  1668|  1668|
  1669|  1669|**Annual:** A plant that completes its life cycle in one growing season.
  1670|  1670|
  1671|  1671|**Crown:** The root mass and growing points of a perennial plant, often divided for propagation.
  1672|  1672|
  1673|  1673|**Division:** The process of splitting a mature perennial plant into smaller sections for propagation.
  1674|  1674|
  1675|  1675|**Forcing:** The practice of encouraging plants to grow earlier than normal, often by excluding light or using warmth.
  1676|  1676|
  1677|  1677|**Polyculture:** Growing multiple crops together in the same space, mimicking natural ecosystems.
  1678|  1678|
  1679|  1679|**Food forest:** A perennial-based planting system that mimics the structure and function of a natural forest.
  1680|  1680|
  1681|  1681|**Oxalic acid:** A compound found in some plants (like spinach and sorrel) that can interfere with calcium absorption and may aggravate kidney stones.
  1682|  1682|
  1683|  1683|**Inulin:** A prebiotic fiber found in Jerusalem artichokes and some other plants, beneficial for gut health.
  1684|  1684|
  1685|  1685|**Blanching:** The practice of excluding light from growing plants to produce tender, pale shoots.
  1686|  1686|
  1687|  1687|---
